.TH "OSTRYA\-INIT" "1" "" "ostrya" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ostrya\-init \- Initialize a new empty repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ostrya init [OPTIONS]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Initialize a new empty repository.
.PP
The command creates the directory at the \%\-\-repo path if it does not exist. The parent directory must exist. Then the command writes the directories of the repository layout and the \fB\%config\fR file. The \fB\%[core]\fR group of \fB\%config\fR holds \fB\%repo_version=1\fR, \fB\%mode\fR, and \fB\%collection\-id\fR if \%\-\-collection\-id is given. With the global option \%\-\-remotes\-config\-dir, the \fB\%[ex\-ostrya]\fR group holds \fB\%remotes\-config\-dir\fR with the absolute path of its value.
.PP
The command creates a new repository only. If the path holds an entry named \fB\%config\fR of any type, the command prints \fB\%error: repository exists: PATH\fR, exits \%1, and writes nothing. In a directory that has entries and no \fB\%config\fR, the command keeps each part of the layout that exists. Without \%\-\-repo, each source of the global option \%\-\-repo gives a repository, so the command refuses it, or prints \fB\%error: Command requires a \-\-repo argument\fR and exits \%1. It prints nothing on success.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fIMODE\fR
The storage mode of the new repository.
.IP
The values are \fB\%archive\fR, \fB\%archive\-z2\fR, \fB\%bare\fR, \fB\%bare\-user\fR, \fB\%bare\-user\-only\fR, and \fB\%bare\-user\-shared\fR\&. \fB\%archive\fR is an alias for \fB\%archive\-z2\fR, and the \fB\%config\fR file records \fB\%archive\-z2\fR\&. \fB\%bare\-user\-shared\fR is an ostrya extension. The command refuses any other value and exits \%1. Default: bare.
.TP
\fB\-\-collection\-id\fR \fICOLLECTION_ID\fR
A globally unique id for this repository as a collection of refs.
.IP
The command writes the value to \fB\%[core] collection\-id\fR in the \fB\%config\fR file. \fB\%commit\fR records this id in the \fB\%ostree.collection\-binding\fR metadata key of each commit, unless \%\-\-no\-bindings is given.
.PP
The global options are listed in \fBostrya\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBostrya\fR(1)
